  "notes": [
    "All four variants ran serially with identical affinity and thread limits on the same shared host; absolute timings can vary with other host workloads.",
    "The notebook was executed from a frozen copy. Its DC extinction-ratio calibration cell was skipped; differential_vpp=2.0 was set directly. The original notebook/helper files were not edited.",
    "Within each comparison, model, source waveform, tolerances, timestep controller, sample timestamps, record length and max_steps were identical. Complete traces include all 998 real/unrolled unknowns.",
    "Fixed-step results compare the original full-history solver with the latest bounded-history solver. Adaptive results compare explicit 1024-slot history with dtmin-inferred history using the latest solver in both cases.",
    "Adaptive PID settings are recorded in variants. dtmin equals the fixed integration timestep, dtmax is four times dtmin, and force_dtmin retains the controller default. Adaptive versus fixed-step runtimes are not presented as an isolated history-sizing speedup.",
    "The 2048-step cold/warm pair uses one stable ODETerm and max_steps=9236. The full records are NRZ 9152 nominal fixed steps and PAM4 9216 nominal fixed steps. No record was shortened or timestep coarsened between either comparison pair.",
    "All calls were synchronized with block_until_ready. Cold call totals include tracing, lowering, compilation and execution. XLA-only compilation is listed separately. Full-record times include their first compilation.",
    "history_bytes counts raw timestamp/state arrays, excluding saved output, executables, process RSS and reverse-mode checkpoints.",
    "These measurements use a 2 Vpp drive and should not be mixed with the earlier 4 Vpp benchmark results."
